// Ch8 B07 "The storm against the wind", first half (act1_ch08.md §2 B07; F08). Letterboxed, scripted.
// The beacon gallery at the crown, looking south-west: the sea has gone the wrong colour. The wind is
// from the land and the cloud is coming the other way (bible §9: it moves against the wind), a wall of
// dark water and cloud lit from inside by wounds. @music silence holds on F08 until the Tender speaks;
// nobody speaks for a long beat. The Tender, panicking, starts the Canticle and gets a line wrong;
// Ysolde quietly gives him the right words, and he steadies (her tell: a correction mid-crisis is her
// warmth). Then the great flue-key is put in Asha's hands: by old Fenn, if she fed the beacon with him
// (ch08_fed_the_beacon; he has climbed after them), else by the Tender. THE PLAYER OPENS IT: the scene
// ends, and the field's interact on the great key plays the second half (ch08_beacon_opened).
// Nothing bound or machine-made is turned against the storm (rule 1): a beacon is a warning.
title: ch08_storm_against_wind
location: ch08/coilspire
---
@letterbox on
@camera F08
@music silence fade=1.0
@sfx wind_landward
@mark asha gallery_asha walk
@mark toma gallery_toma walk
@mark ysolde gallery_ysolde walk
@mark liss gallery_liss walk
@wait 4.0
@anim tender palms_level
Tender [afraid]: Be level, be still, the Hush is over the water and the water— the water is— #line:ch08_storm_001
@wait 0.8
Ysolde [tender]: "...and the water is kept." Go on. You have it. #line:ch08_storm_002
Tender [afraid]: And the water is kept. And the keeping is still. #line:ch08_storm_003
@wait 1.0
<<if $ch08_fed_the_beacon>>
@anim fenn hand_key asha
Fenn [neutral]: You know the way of her now. #line:ch08_storm_004
<<else>>
@anim tender hand_key asha
Tender [afraid]: The great key, Lady Cantor. It has to be a Cantor's hand. #line:ch08_storm_005
<<endif>>
@camera F08_key
@wait 1.0
@letterbox off
===
